{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event is a value conforming to "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a value: tracking an event records it as an "},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with its timestamp, the caller’s "},{"code":"SourceLocation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as one of the tracker’s "},{"code":"records","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Delivering is a chain of operators over that sequence: Afluent’s "},{"code":"batch(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"batch()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the default) gathers the records into batches, and "},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hands each batch to every destination, as a lazy unit of work. A "},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a plain sink, narrowed or transformed by its modifiers: "},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"code":"redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"droppingCallSite()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A tracker given a "},{"code":"Consent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" delivers an event only once the user grants its "},{"code":"ConsentCategory","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", holding it while undecided and dropping it when denied. "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" only queues an event, from any thread; a worker the tracker owns, never on the main actor, does the rest. A tracker given a "},{"code":"SegmentStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" writes each record to disk as its worker reaches it and delivers what an earlier run left first. A property whose valid values are narrower than its type is a "},{"code":"Refined","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value, which satisfies its "},{"code":"Refinement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s "},{"code":"Constraint","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s from the moment it is made, or carries constraints declared with "},{"code":"@Constrained","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the tracker’s worker rejects an event that breaks one before anything else, reporting each as a "},{"code":"RejectionReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"rejectionReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". On Apple platforms, SwiftUI views read the tracker from the environment and track what they do with view modifiers, and a screen’s events carry its "},{"code":"ScreenKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). UIKit views and view controllers inherit it as a trait, the same value as SwiftUI’s, set on a window scene ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and AppKit views find it up their responder chain ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"); a control’s "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks an event through the tracker found when its action fires, so each scene or window can have its own. Screen views can track themselves once a window scene or window turns it on with "},{"code":"trackScreensAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"code":"ScreenViewed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as each screen’s view controller appears, without swizzling ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), and UIKit controls once a window scene turns it on with "},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which tracks "},{"code":"ControlActivated","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as a touch activates each control named by its accessibility identifier ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). On every platform, "},{"code":"trackLifecycle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tracks the app’s installs, updates, opens, moves to the background and terminations, and makes the tracker’s records durable as it leaves the foreground ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given the "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" enricher stamps every event with its session’s "},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a random identifier held in memory only, and starts a new session after a timeout of inactivity, tracking "},{"code":"SessionEnded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracker given "},{"code":"Sampler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s keeps a seeded fraction of the events they apply to, event by event, or whole sessions with "},{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", dropping the rest on its worker before they are held, written or delivered, reporting each drop as a "},{"code":"SamplingDropReport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and stamping each kept record with its "},{"code":"SampleRateKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The standard enrichers, "},{"code":"Enricher.application()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"device()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"operatingSystem()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"locale()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"network()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"vendorIdentifier()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", stamp every event with the app, device, operating system, locale, network connection and the platform’s identifier for vendor, each under a typed key, the static ones read once ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module but "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a product of its own for apps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that already use GRDB; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" macro derives an event’s conformances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and schema from its declaration and which alone builds swift-syntax; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exports those schemas as a JSON Schema tracking plan and checks the events against a committed one;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which runs that check from an app’s tests; and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"code":"withRecordingTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives a test’s body a fresh tracker and returns what it tracked. Each module also has its own documentation and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","struct SignedUp: Event {","    var plan: String","}","","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: ConsoleDestination())","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"Traffluent","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"externalID":"Traffluent","symbolKind":"module"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"anchor":"Essentials"},{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"],"anchor":"Guides"},{"title":"Choosing what to record","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests"],"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"},{"title":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums"],"anchor":"Modules"},{"title":"Testing","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"],"anchor":"Testing"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"LoggingDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Automatic Tracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","type":"topic"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","url":"\/documentation\/events","type":"topic"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","title":"CollectorEncoding","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"TrackingPlans","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","type":"topic"},"doc://AutomaticScreenTracking/documentation/AutomaticScreenTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticscreentracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticScreenTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticScreenTracking","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"AutomaticScreenTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Tracking Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","type":"topic"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"kind":"symbol","title":"TracingDestinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"abstract":[{"text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Consent Gating","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","type":"topic"},"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Sessions","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","url":"\/documentation\/sessions","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftUITracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://StandardContext/documentation/StandardContext":{"kind":"symbol","title":"StandardContext","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext","url":"\/documentation\/standardcontext","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackertesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"TrackerTesting","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"kind":"article","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"EventMacros","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros","url":"\/documentation\/eventmacros","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"kind":"article","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","abstract":[{"text":"Export the JSON Schema of every event an app tracks, commit it, and fail the build when the events stop matching it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Checksums/documentation/Checksums":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Checksums","identifier":"doc:\/\/Checksums\/documentation\/Checksums","url":"\/documentation\/checksums","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChoosingDestinations":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Choosing Destinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://LifecycleTracking/documentation/LifecycleTracking":{"kind":"symbol","title":"LifecycleTracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking","url":"\/documentation\/lifecycletracking","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PrivacyManifests":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"role":"article","title":"Privacy Manifests","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/privacymanifests","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"kind":"article","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/PersistingRecords":{"kind":"article","title":"Persisting Records","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so a record the app tracked survives the process ending."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PersistingRecords","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"kind":"symbol","title":"Traffluent","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/WhatGoesWhere":{"kind":"article","title":"Logging, Tracing, Metrics and Analytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four signals, four jobs. Decide which one a fact belongs to before you write the line that records it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/whatgoeswhere","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"AutomaticControlTracking","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"UIKitTracking","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SamplingEvents":{"abstract":[{"text":"Keep a seeded fraction of the events a tracker tracks, event by event or a whole session at once.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Sampling Events","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SamplingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","type":"topic"},"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"Destinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","url":"\/documentation\/destinations","type":"topic"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"kind":"symbol","title":"GRDBPersistence","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/documentation\/GRDBPersistence","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Changing an Event","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","type":"topic"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"kind":"symbol","title":"AppKitTracking","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/DefiningEvents":{"abstract":[{"text":"Derive an event’s conformances and schema from its declaration with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and constrain which values its properties may hold.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Defining Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/DefiningEvents","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/IdentifyingPeople":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent knows people only by a pseudonymous session. An identifier that outlives one is yours to add, store, reset and gate with consent."}],"role":"article","title":"Identifying People","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/identifyingpeople","type":"topic"},"doc://Trackers/documentation/Trackers":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackers","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trackers\/documentation\/Trackers","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Trackers","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence":{"abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"Persistence","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","url":"\/documentation\/persistence","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/SessionsAndStandardContext":{"kind":"article","title":"Sessions and Standard Context","abstract":[{"text":"Stamp every event with its session and with the app, device, system, locale and network it was tracked on.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/SessionsAndStandardContext","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"}}}